---
term: Audit
section: accountability
order: 20
definition: An independent review of whether a corporation, its executive, or its measurement system is performing as the charter requires.
seeAlso:
  - measurement-mechanism
  - delegation-of-functions
  - rules-as-code
  - fidelity-audit
---
A charter can include audit triggers that start an audit automatically, for example when a metric crosses a threshold. The entity under audit can't choose, dismiss, or replace its auditor.

Auditors rotate often, so no auditor serves long enough to start accommodating the entity it reviews.
